within one whole day; as close of day, ׳עַדלֿ 2Chr 35:14 ; as time of sacred חָג (לֵיל) Isa 30:29 ; of suffering and weeping עָמָל לֵילוֺת Job 7:3 , compare Psa 6:7 ; 77:3 etc.; of pious desires, prayer, praise, meditation, etc (sometimes || by day ) Isa 26:9 ; Job 35:10 ; Psa 1:2 ; 22:3 ; 42:9 ; 77:7 ; 88:2 ; 92:3 ; 119:5 (twice in verse), compare 16:7 ; 17:8 ; of night-service in Temple 134:1 ; of sudden assault, or destruction, Isa 15:1 ; Jer 6:5 ; Obadiah 5; Job 27:20 ; 34:20 , 25 ; 36:20 ; divided into watches Psa 90:4 ; שִׁמֻּרִים לֵיל Exod 12:42 see below שׁמר ; with number, denoting duration of time, forty days and forty nights Gen 7:4 , 12 ; Exod 24:18 ; 34:28 ; Deut 9:9 , 11 , 18 , 25 ; 10:10 ; 1Kin 19:8 ; three days and three nights ( לֵילוֺת שְׁלשָׁה ) 1Sam 30:12 ; Jonah 2:1 ; seven days and seven nights ( לֵילוֺת שִׁבְעַת ) Job 2:13 ; הַלּ ׳חֲלוֺם Gen 20:3 ; 31:24 (both E), 1Kin 3:5 ; הַלּ ׳מַרְאֹת Gen 46:2 (E); ל ׳חֶזְיוֺן Job 20:8 ; 33:15 , ל ׳חֶזְיֹנוֺת 4:13 , ל חֲזוֺן ׳חֲלוֺם Isa 29:7 (compare Micah 3:6 below) ; ׳בִּןלֿ Jonah 4:10 (twice in verse) see בֵּן 8 b. Chiefly in adverb. phrase: — הַלּ ׳בַּחֲצִי at midnight Exod 12:29 + (see חָצוֺת חֲצִי, b), compare הַלּ ׳בְּתוֺךְ 1Kin 3:20 , ל ׳בְּאִישׁוֺן Prov 7:9 ; ׳בַּלּ הַזֶּה Exod 12:8 , 12 on this night (P; the night of which one is speaking); ׳בַּלּ הַהוּא on that night Gen 19:35 (J) + often, (P only Num 14:1 ); ׳בַּל הוּא Gen 19:33 ; 30:16 ; so ׳הַלּ alone 1Sam 14:34 , but strike out ᵐ5 We Kit, compare Dr; Klo Bu read ליהוה ; ׳הַלּ to-night Gen 19:5 , 34 ; 30:15 (all J), Num 22:8 , 19 (E), Josh 2:2 ; 4:3 (both J E), 2Sam 17:1 , 16 ; 19:8 ; Ruth 1:12 ; 3:2 , 13 , opposed to מָחָר tomorrow 1Sam 19:11 ; ׳הַלּ = this night just past, last night 15:16 (compare Dr); ׳כָּלהַֿלּ all night Hosea 7:6 (opposed to בֹּקֶר ), Exod 14:20-21 , (J), Num 11:32 ; Josh 10:9 (both J E), Judg 16:2 (twice in verse); 19:25 ; 1Sam 15:11 ; 31:12 ; 2Sam 2:29 , 32 ; 4:7 ; opposed to ההוא כלהֿיום (of continuous action) 1Sam 19:24 ; 28:20 ; Isa 62:6 , opposed to יומם Psa 78:14 ; ׳בְּכָללֿ 6:7 every night (probably); compare כָּלהַֿלֵּילוֺת Isa 21:8 all the nights (opposed to יוֺמָם ) ; especially לַיְלָה by night Num 22:20 (E) Josh 8:3 (JE), Deut 16:1 ; Num 9:16 (P) + 51 t.; of these Gen 14:15 and Exod 13:21-22 , (J) + 25 t. opposed to יוֺמָם , covering all the time; otherwise Judg 6:27 (opposed to יוֺמָם ); וָיוֺם לַיְלָה night and day 1Kin 8:29 ; Isa 27:3 ; Est 4:16 ; less often לֵילוֺת Psalm 16:17; ׳הַלּ by night 2Kin 25:4 ( ׳ל in || Jer 52:7 ), Zech 1:8 ; Neh 4:16 (opposed to הַיּוֺם ) ; ׳בַּלּ id., Jer 6:5 18 t. (chiefly late; often opposed to יוֺמָם בַּיּוֺם, , etc.); בַּלֵּילוֺת Psa 92:3 (opposed to בַּבֹּקֶר , 134:1 ; Song 3:1 , 8 ; בְּלַיְלָה Neh 9:19 (opposed to בְּיוֺמָם ); בְּלֵיל Isa 15:1 (twice in verse) ׳כַּל as at night Job 5:14 (opposed to צָהֳרָ֑יִם ). 2 figurative צִלֵּךְ כַּלַיִל שִׁיתִי Isa 16:8 simile of shadow of Zion as protection; more often in gloomy sense, of avenging calamity without divine guidance or comfort מֵחָזוֺן לַיְלָה Micah 3:6 ; personal distress Job 35:10 ; judgment perhaps also 36:20 (Ew De Di Da; night of death Bu; 'unintelligible' Siegf); מַהמִּֿלֵּיל מַהמִּֿלַּיְלָה Isa 21:11 i.e. what hour of the night of calamity is it? compare 21:12 (opposed to בֹּקֶר ). [ לֵילָא ] noun [masculine] night (see Biblical Hebrew לַ֫יְלָה ); — emphatic לֵילְיָא Dan 2:19 ; 5:30 ; 7:2 , 7 , 13 .","rootNote":"or (Isaiah 21:11) לֵיל ; also לַיְלָה ; from the same as 3883 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 33","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 33","1Chr 17 3","1Kgs 3 5","1Kgs 3 19","1Kgs 3 20","1Kgs 8 29","1Kgs 8 59","1Kgs 19 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":235,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 9 33","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/לַ֛יְלָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 17 3","book":"1Chr","cha